  merger: {status: 'Special committees of independent directors formed at both Tesla and SpaceX to review a merger (confirmed by Musk on SpaceX’s Q3 call, 20 Oct 2026). Tesla’s Q3 10-Q (22 Oct): the committee is exploring “deepening Tesla’s relationship with SpaceX”, possibly a business combination; no assurance of a deal. SpaceX’s 10-Q: a deal would need Musk’s approval as SpaceX’s controlling holder. Bloomberg (22 Oct): advisers target an announcement in 1H 2027 (not confirmed by either company). Reuters (22 Oct): both sides have hired advisers; talks early-stage. 25 Oct: a retail shareholder letter (6,493 self-reported signers, 17.5m shares) urges a vote once terms are set; due to be sent 26 Oct. 26 Oct: Barclays upgraded TSLA on deal expectations and sees an all-stock SpaceX acquisition as the most likely structure (analyst view; neither company has announced terms).', terms: null, vote: 'Yes votes from 50% of all outstanding Tesla shares', src: U.merger}
